[[2047,96,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The optional services relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J60</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls\nthe heating circuit for the seats as well as the electric rear windows\nand sun roof \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234128\">E3060</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,</p><p>The coil for relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J60 is energized when\nthe ignition is switched on (INT/A) by the line for fuse F6 of supplementary\nfuse box B98 B, whilst the supply at the relay contact arrives from\nthe battery, through the line for maxifuse J/B2 of B99.</strong></p><p>This supply passes through fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              of\nsupplementary fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 C</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which guarantees the protection\nof the circuit and reaches the switches in the seats through connection \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>D70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (left seat) and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>D71</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (right seat): the supply for\nthe two devices is therefore controlled by the ignition (INT/A)\nand they are connected to earth.</p><p>By pressing the switch on the seat the resistors\nfor the heaters in the left and right seats, \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>040 and 041, connected\nin parallel, are supplied, until a thermal contact inside the heaters\ndisconnects the resistors when the temperature exceeds a certain\nlimit.</strong></p><p>When the resistors are on, an LED signals\nthe operation of the device.</p>"]]